# Normalise line endings in the repository, not on the developer's machine.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf enabled would rewrite the
# LF endings in tracked text, and `pnpm pack` would then ship a tarball whose
# contents differ from the one built on Linux. Pinning `eol=lf` makes the packed
# README, LICENSE and cordis.patch.yml byte-identical across platforms, which is
# what lets the release tarball be verified on one machine and trusted on another.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be converted; a changed byte corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.tgz binary

# Lockfiles are machine-generated and must stay byte-stable.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf -diff

